# White Ward's "This effect doesn't remove this Aura" spares it from its own protection only: another source of
# protection from white still removes it (CR 702.16n, 704.5m). White Ward is white, so it cannot be cast onto a creature
# that already has protection from white (CR 702.16b; that is why Black Knight is refused in the enchant scenario), but
# a creature can get its own later. Bot1's White Knight wears White Ward, which stays at first (the Knight has only
# protection from black). Sleight of Mind then changes "black" in the Knight's text to "white" (CR 612.2): the Knight's
# own protection from white is no part of the Ward's effect, and the Aura is put into Bot1's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
White Knight
White Ward
Sleight of Mind
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.White Knight.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.White Ward.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.White Knight)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.White Ward.AttachedTo = White Knight
? Bot1.Battlefield.White Knight.ProtectionFrom = Black; White
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sleight of Mind.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.White Knight)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Colors(Black)
Bot1.Colors(White)
[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = White Ward; Sleight of Mind
Bot1.Battlefield.White Knight.ProtectionFrom = White
